    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n45349" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Stercŭlĭus</span></b> ,
		ii, m.
		stercus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the deity that presides over manuring</i>,
					<i><span class="en">Tert. Apol. 25</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Macr. S. 1, 7</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Lact. 1, 20 <i>fin.</i></span></i>; <i><span class="en">1, 36</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Serv.
				Verg. G. 1, 21</span></i>.—Called also, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Stercŭ-lus</span></b> , Prud.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στεφ</span>. 2, 450; <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Stercŭtus</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Stercŭtĭus</span></b> ,
				<i><span class="en">Plin.
				17, 9, 6, § 50</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Lact. 1,
				20, 36</span></i>; and, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Stercenĭus</span></b> , <i><span class="en">Serv.
				Verg. A. 11, 850</span></i>; cf. Aug. Civ. Dei, 18, 15; and Becker,
			Ant. 4, p. 16.</div>
